  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:5677",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is implicated in the relationship with JM1 through a series of molecular interactions involving sialyltransferase activity. The evidence suggests that Castanospermine acts as a target for CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is subsequently targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and 1-Hydroxycyclocolorenone. These intermediates all ultimately target JM1, indicating a chain of enzymatic interactions that culminate in the modulation of JM1. The presence of multiple pathways converging on JM1 through different targets highlights a potential mechanism where Castanospermine influences JM1 via a complex network of enzymatic activities, possibly through the regulation of sialyltransferase function. This integrated pathway underscores the role of sialyltransferase in mediating the effects of Castanospermine on JM1, suggesting a broader biological context where these interactions may contribute to cellular processes.",
